        "explanation": "Explanation:\nQuery 111: The array to consider is [3,−1,2][3, -1, 2][3,−1,2]. It's optimal to choose the triple of indices (1,3,2)(1, 3, 2)(1,3,2), which turns the array into [6][6][6] (since A1+A3−A2=3+2−(−1)=6A_1+A_3-A_2 = 3+2-(-1) = 6A1​+A3​−A2​=3+2−(−1)=6).\nThis is optimal.\nQuery 222: The array to consider is [3][3][3]. No operations can be performed, and the answer is just 333.\nQuery 333: Now, we consider the full array. One optimal sequence of moves is:\n\nChoose (2,3,1)(2, 3, 1)(2,3,1), turning the array into [4,5,−2][4, 5, -2][4,5,−2].\nChoose (1,2,3)(1, 2, 3)(1,2,3), turning the array into [11][11][11]."
